"## Summary\n\nAgent-core follow-ups 37 to 43, on one branch, merged together.\n- **Sessions:** 37 started at 00:37 EST on 2026-11-03 on #401's tip `05b2c2f2`, and 43 delivered at 13:07 EST.\n- **Models:** 37 ran on agy `claude-opus-5-5-high`. 38 to 43 ran on codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 65 non-merge commits and 95 owned files against `main` `567080be`. Merge-tree is clean and prepush-scan is clean.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **What this carries:** seven follow-ups. Six of them judged and fixed adversarial reviews r20 to r25 of the agent's restart, adoption, usage attribution, Boot, retention and expiry paths, plus netlab's F32-01.\n  - Every finding was judged before its fix (D-141): its proof ran on the base first.\n  - Review r26 then reviewed the final production tree, and found nothing.\n- **Per follow-up:**\n  - **37, review r20 of #401** (2 High, 3 Medium, 1 Low; H-2 went to netlab 27).\n    - **Confirmed and fixed:** H-1, M-1, M-2 and M-3.\n      - A refused same-boot adoption settles the retained usage.\n      - A TERM during Boot completes a bounded baseline.\n      - The generation, clock and set checks run before the node lock and the probe.\n      - A withdrawing hand-off writes the heartbeat.\n    - **Rejected:** L-1, as unreachable and harmless. It is kept as guards.\n  - **38, review r21 of 37** (2 High, 2 Medium, 1 Low). Every finding was confirmed and fixed:\n    - **H-1** (introduced by 37): Boot snapshots the desired state before the refresh, reads the live generation, and settles only identities common to both.\n    - **H-2:** refresh and Apply wait until the final settlement closes the retained interval.\n    - **M-1:** open and closed epochs.\n    - **M-2:** one 10 s Boot budget, a bounded worker and a 3 s `Close`.\n    - **L-1.**\n  - **39, review r22 of 38** (2 High, 3 Medium).\n    - **Confirmed and fixed:** H-1 A/B, H-2.1 to H-2.5, M-1, M-2's ordering and M-3 A/B/C.\n    - **Rejected, with guards kept:** H-1 B's paused-sampling sub-claim, and M-2's original trace.\n  - **40, review r23 of 39** (3 High, 1 Medium, 1 Low).\n    - **Confirmed and fixed:** H-1c, H-2, H-3a/b/b' and M-1.\n    - **Confirmed in part:** H-1a.\n    - **A provenance limitation:** H-1b, with its labelled guard kept.\n    - **Clarified:** L-1.\n  - **41, review r24's H-1 and H-3.** r24 reviewed netlab 31's hand-over design, and returned these two agent findings to this lane.\n    - **H-1:** a healthy, unchanged 304 tick no longer runs a full Apply. The model and pending work are compared under the node lock, serving and the member path are verified fresh, and the verifier checks element completeness.\n    - **H-3:** each binding keeps its own `ValidUntil` cap.\n    - r24's H-1 fixture was corrected to a genuine 304, by an orchestrator-approved setup-only change.\n  - **42, review r25 of 41** (1 High, 1 Medium), and netlab's F32-01.\n    - **H-1:** a sibling binding's deadline no longer withdraws the whole node. The fix has three parts:\n      - two deadlines, the earliest wake and the last installed binding's deadline, which the heartbeat, Boot, adoption and the watchdog use;\n      - an Apply of the surviving bindings on the same tick;\n      - an expired-only removal fast path.\n    - **M-1:** retention survives an epoch rotation.\n    - **F32-01:** uniform millisecond renewal jitter, persisted.\n    - The only `node/enforce` change is the `DeadlineMono` comment.\n  - **43:**\n    - r26's six proofs were imported, and `main` was merged once.\n    - The owed D-133 A,B,A,B ran in two reservations, and no leg qualified (below).\n    - The ordinary B lab gate passed all 13 scenarios, D087 / D104 included. It ran after both reservations were released.\n    - Every other gate passed, including plain `go test ./...`.\n    - No production change.\n- **Review r26** (agy `gemini-4-argon-high`) reviewed 42 at `8dec4100`, and 37 to 42 together.\n  - **Findings:** 0 Critical, 0 High, 0 Medium, 0 Low.\n  - **Its recommendation